timation & budgeting</h3><p>Preliminary cost estimates, materials schedules, budget proposals, and expenditure tracking.</p></div><div class="card rv"><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12l5-5 4 2 4-2 5 5-5 5-3-2-3 2-4-2-3-3z"/><path d="M9 14l3 2"/></svg></span><h3>Contractor coordination</h3><p>Coordinating contractors, suppliers, milestones, and communication among authorised project stakeholders.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap split"><div class="rv"><span class="eyebrow">Institutional capacity, seamless execution</span><h2>Construction project lifecycle</h2><ol class="check" style="counter-reset:l"><li>Client consultation and initial project brief</li><li>Site assessment and requirements definition</li><li>Design and technical professional engagement, where required</li><li>Scope of work, budget, schedule, and proposal</li><li>Contract preparation and agreement</li><li>Procurement and mobilisation planning</li><li>Construction or renovation execution</li><li>Progress monitoring and approved variations</li><li>Inspection, snag resolution, and handover</li><li>Final reporting and project closure</li></ol></div>
<div class="rv"><div class="notice rv"><b>Two engagement types.</b> We distinguish between a contract executed by Clapet and an assignment where the company only provides supervision or consultancy. Each project carries a unique reference, signed agreement, approved scope, schedule, cost baseline, change log and completion documents.</div></div></div></section>
<section class=""><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head rv center"><span class="eyebrow">How it works</span><h2>How a construction assignment runs</h2></div><div class="steps "><div class="step rv"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Consultation & brief</h3><p>We understand the project type, intended use, location, size, stage, budget and timeline.</p></div><div class="step rv"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Assessment & proposal</h3><p>Site assessment, scope of work, cost baseline and schedule are agreed in writing.</p></div><div class="step rv"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Contract & mobilisation</h3><p>Agreement signed, suppliers and contractors coordinated, mobilisation planned.</p></div><div class="step rv"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Execution & monitoring</h3><p>Work proceeds with progress monitoring and approved variations only.</p></div><div class="step rv"><div class="n">05</div><h3>Handover & close-out</h3><p>Inspection, snag resolution, completion documents and final report.</p></div></div></div></section>


